{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791797408,"nonce":"EJGsThYkiqs8f9n9NPGSEK1qXCw=","message":"Startup-path investigation (2026-10-12): audited xwindow window_open/open_waiting, macOS appkit::serve, winit applicationDidFinishLaunching and NSWindow creation, SDK NativeWindowHost initialization/render scheduling, and native/src/window_pump.rs. xwindow pumps until it has created a window after resume; winit orders it visible with makeKeyAndOrderFront, but creation does not wait for NSWindowOcclusionStateVisible. Initial Occluded events are change notifications; no initial true snapshot is synthesized. SDK opens the window, sets DeviceEvents.Never, enables the external libuv pump, then asynchronously creates the adapter/device and finally the surface. With external pumping enabled, Window.poll only drains queues; the libuv check callback drives AppKit. Therefore JS retry timers alone do not establish that the native platform pump remains healthy during historical stalls.\n\nBuilt an isolated diagnostic SDK addon from current published sources (main trees untouched). It logs exact xgpu acquisition status and exposes read-only snapshots for our own NSWindow (occlusionState, isVisible, isOnActiveSpace, level), NSApplication (active/hidden/launched/policy), and native bridge counters (checks, queue/pending skips, actual pump calls, notifications/callback completions). Four alternating bridge/polling pairs all presented; later fresh-process bridge and polling runs each presented three windows. In the fresh bridge process, first frame arrived at 491ms total (GPU ready 472ms), later windows 49/56ms; bridge counters advanced to checks=19,pumps=16,notifications=callbacks=6,pendingSkips=0. Fresh polling first frame 373ms total, later windows 84/56ms. All observed failed acquisitions were Occluded. Native windows began with occlusionState=8192 (visible bit clear) and recovered to 8194; GPU readiness can precede this transition. An xwindow-only probe, with no GPU instance/device/surface, recovered the same state with both bridge and polling; cold bridge exposure was 554ms including open. Some initial isOnActiveSpace reads were false, including an exposed xwindow-only snapshot, so that getter alone is not proof of the old Space/fullscreen hypothesis.\n\nActual native-host, native-scene-window and native-idle regressions passed against the instrumented addon. Idle reports idlePolls=0, idleFrames=0, wake=140ms, multiple-window/recreate checks pass. Scene test setup first needed its example and tsconfig staged in the isolated directory; those setup failures were not native failures. No sustained first-frame stall reproduced. Current evidence confirms asynchronous AppKit exposure and successful retry/wake behavior in these runs; it does not rule out a rare bridge stall or explain the historical 60-second failures. Isolated tests now sample native state plus bridge counters once per second while awaiting a first frame, ready to capture the next occurrence without changing production timeouts. Directory /private/tmp/blinc-first-frame-startup; logs startup-probe.log, startup-cold-bridge.log, startup-cold-polling.log, xwindow-only.log, native-host-final.log, native-scene-window-instrumented.log, native-idle-instrumented.log.","files":null}]}